{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "0f12b1a9-7c69-51d1-ab4a-ad4778d97aeb",
  "Description": "A torus volume pulls 300 boxes onto its own surface.\n\nOne [VolumePrimitive] is used twice. Meshed by [VolumeToMesh] it is the collider. Through the Vectors output of [VolumeToField] it is a force: the gradient of a level set points away from the surface, so a [RigidForce] of type Field with a negative Strength pulls bodies towards it. World gravity is off.\n\nAKA: vector field, gradient, attract, magnet, field force, volume force\n\nTips\n- The pull only reaches as far as the level set's band, so BandWidth on [VolumePrimitive] is the reach of the force.\n- A positive Strength turns the volume into a repeller.\n- A volume with a stored vector grid, such as a cached velocity, drives the bodies along that grid instead.",
